' ai_sandbox.rr: a run RAI or an AI app starts is sandboxed — try it.
'
'   rapidr run ai_sandbox.rr
'
' Run it yourself (F5 in RapidR Studio, or the line above): it starts
' another program with SHELLWAIT, as any program may, and says how that
' went. Then ask RAI "run ai_sandbox.rr" (or let an AI app run it): Studio
' runs the programs an AI starts sandboxed, so SHELL, SHELLWAIT, RUN, a DLL
' call (DECLARE … LIB) and SENDMESSAGE stop it with an error that says
' why — unless you turned on Tools > Settings > AI > "Programs the AI runs
' may use DLLs and SHELL". Files, the network and the program's own
' windows work as usual either way. Nothing here changes a file.
' (docs/manual/ai-assistant.md, "Privacy and safety")

DIM Sandbox AS STRING
DIM Code AS INTEGER

Sandbox = ENVIRON$("RAPIDR_SANDBOX")
IF Sandbox <> "" AND Sandbox <> "0" THEN
  PRINT "This run is sandboxed: an AI started it."
  PRINT "The next line stops the program with an error that says why."
ELSE
  PRINT "This run has your own Run's power: it may start other programs."
END IF

PRINT "Starting another program with SHELLWAIT..."
Code = SHELLWAIT("echo Hello from another program")
PRINT "It ended with exit code "; Code
